#sec("IV", "Engineering and Scientific Applications")

#subsec("A", "Primary Application Domains and Mathematical Fit")

1. *Satellite Remote Sensing and Crop Phenology Classification*: Multi-temporal NDVI vegetation curves for identical crop species experience local temporal stretching due to regional sowing-date delays and microclimate growing-degree-day fluctuations @petitjean2011dba. DBA natively handles variable acquisition lengths and produces interpretable phenological prototype curves preserving peak greenness amplitudes.
2. *Speech Recognition and Spoken-Word Prototype Learning*: Utterances of the same word vary nonlinearly in vowel elongation and consonant transition duration across speakers @sakoe1978dtw. DBA constructs sharp acoustic template centroids without smearing formant peaks, avoiding the amplitude blurring caused by Euclidean averaging.
3. *Human Motion Capture, Gait, and Gesture Clustering*: Inertial measurement unit (IMU) trajectories and skeletal joint-angle series vary in execution speed across repetitions and subjects. Elastic warping absorbs speed modulation while preserving absolute joint angles and excursion magnitudes, which $z$-normalized methods like k-Shape discard.
4. *Industrial Batch-Process Monitoring (Chemical & Semiconductor)*: Temperature, pressure, and reactant concentration trajectories across batch runs undergo variable reaction induction times and cooling rates. DBA extracts canonical "golden batch" reference profiles against which anomalous process drifts are detected.
5. *Biomedical ICU Vital-Sign and Physiological Trajectory Analysis*: Hemodynamic response curves and post-intervention vital-sign trajectories evolve at patient-specific rates. Because DBA preserves clinical units (mmHg, bpm) and admits variable-length trajectories without artificial truncation, clinicians can inspect cluster barycenters directly.

#subsec("B", "Failure Modes and Domain Suitability Matrix")

DBA encounters four principal failure modes: (i) *pathological singularities*, where unconstrained warping maps a single centroid point to an entire flat plateau of a series, mitigated via Sakoe-Chiba band constraints (Proposition 2); (ii) *initialization-induced local minima*, demonstrated constructively in Theorem 2 where Euclidean-mean seeding stalls immediately at $4 times$ the global cost (favoring medoid or $k$-Means++ seeding); (iii) *severe outlier sensitivity*, as a single corrupted trajectory breaks the barycenter ($epsilon^ast = 1 / |C_k|$, Proposition 1); and (iv) *quadratic scaling for long series* ($m > 10^4$), where unconstrained $O(m^2)$ DP becomes prohibitive compared to k-Shape (Alg. 162) or ROCKET-Clustering (Alg. 165).

